          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em genus
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            (2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            that helps classify the surface’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            class. It gives the number of handles or ‘cross caps’ that are in a sum decomposition of the surface.
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+geometry"} complex analytic geometry
            a surface, being complex 1-dimensional, is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+curves"} complex curves
            and so one speaks of the
            = succeed "." do
